  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef has 444 positive integers AAA, BBB, CCC, and DDD such that AAA %\\%% B=CB=CB=C %\\%% DDD.\n\nFind the **smallest positive** integer XXX such that (A+X)(A+X)(A+X) %\\%% B=(C+X)B=(C+X)B=(C+X) %\\%% DDD holds.\n\nIt is guaranteed that such XXX always exists.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nThe first and only line of each test case contains four space-separated integers AAA, BBB, CCC, and DDD.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, print a single line containing one integer — XXX, the smallest integer satisfying the conditions.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤A,B,C,D≤1091 \\leq A, B, C, D \\leq 10^91≤A,B,C,D≤109",
      "AAA %\\%% B=CB = CB=C %\\%% DDD"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n4 7 4 8\n5 1 8 2\n3 2 4 3",
        "output": "1\n2\n5",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: The smallest XXX satisfying the equation is 111, as (4+1)(4+1)(4+1) %\\%% 7=(4+1)7=(4+1)7=(4+1) %\\%% 8=58 = 58=5.\nTest case 222: The smallest XXX satisfying the equation is 222, as (5+2)(5+2)(5+2) %\\%% 1=(8+2)1=(8+2)1=(8+2) %\\%% 2=02 = 02=0."
      }
    ]
  },
